33
00:01:27.174 --> 00:01:29.710
the original variety show and so,

34
00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.240
and I have never stopped since.

35
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.163
And I'm so, I feel so blessed.

36
00:01:34.252 --> 00:01:35.085
(Marie laughing)

37
00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:36.463
My God, I love you.

38
00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.250
I really, really do

39
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:44.510
and there's a couple aspects about motherhood

40
00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:48.610
that also really was important for me

41
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:51.800
and I got excited about talking to you about.

42
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.770
I would love to start with your mother

43
00:01:54.653 --> 00:01:59.653
and ask about how she kept you guys level headed.

44
00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.160
She, okay, for example, Donny and Marie.

45
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.210
Okay, I was, I believe I was around 16 years old

46
00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.530
and I had come home and you put hours in,

47
00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.070
I was doing 15 hours a day, six days a week,

48
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.890
sometimes 18 hours,

49
00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:16.670
working through the child welfare laws

50
00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:19.540
and going to school and learning 350 pages of script

51
00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.200
in two and a half days.

52
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.040
And I remember one time I came home

53
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.090
and it was the next day was the taping.

54
00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.463
I said, "Mom, I'm so tired.

55
00:02:27.662 --> 00:02:29.790
"I have to get to sleep so that I look good on camera".

56
00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.060
And she goes, "Well, you haven't done your chores".

57
00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.567
And I said, "Hello, like

58
00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.937
"our show is dubbed into 17 languages worldwide.

59
00:02:36.937 --> 00:02:38.770
"And I'm like, you know, Marie Osmond".

60
00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:42.210
And she, that was the worst thing I ever could have said,

61
00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.697
'cause she goes, "Oh I see.

62
00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.257
"So now you're going to do your chores and the toilets

63
00:02:47.257 --> 00:02:50.467
"and if you make another word complaining,

64
00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:53.080
"I have a lot more for you to do".

65
00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.677
And she said, "Because you have to realize that's a job.

66
00:02:55.677 --> 00:02:56.987
"Jobs will come and go.

67
00:02:56.987 --> 00:02:58.267
"This is reality.

68
00:02:58.267 --> 00:02:59.617
"This is what will always be here.

69
00:02:59.617 --> 00:03:00.740
"Now get to work".

70
00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.243
And Drew throughout my life this woman,

71
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.937
she said, I'd come home and she'd say,

72
00:03:05.937 --> 00:03:07.497
"Okay, now we're going to learn to make bread.

73
00:03:07.497 --> 00:03:09.497
"Now we're gonna learn to make clothing"

74
00:03:10.641 --> 00:03:12.730
And I'd be like "Mom I have designers and people that sew"

75
00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:13.563
and she goes "Exactly.

76
00:03:13.563 --> 00:03:15.157
"That's why you're going to learn to do it".

77
00:03:16.398 --> 00:03:17.231
And she just,

78
00:03:17.231 --> 00:03:18.390
I mean, she taught me how to gut a fish,

79
00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:20.980
in case I was camping and I needed to cook it.

80
00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.450
This woman taught me reality.

81
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.147
My mom told me once she goes, "I don't care if you hate me.

82
00:03:26.147 --> 00:03:28.766
"If you do that means I'm doing a good job".

83
00:03:28.766 --> 00:03:31.000
Yes, yes, yes.

84
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.690
I couldn't agree more

85
00:03:33.748 --> 00:03:38.300
and something else that has to do with mothers,

86
00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:42.550
that I really loved about your story was,

87
00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.230
when I had kids of my own,

88
00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.500
I felt like, oh my God,

89
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.150
I don't want to pretend to be other people.

90
00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:49.990
My kids need me.

91
00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:54.990
Those 18 hour days no longer seem like a good idea

92
00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:57.100
for me right now.

93
00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.030
I've been doing them my whole life, so it was,

94
00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.410
I had a luxury of saying,

95
00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.910
I'm ready to prioritize my children over work.

96
00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.144
Right.

97
00:04:06.144 --> 00:04:06.977
But then I had to earn a living,

98
00:04:06.977 --> 00:04:08.330
so I had to figure stuff out,

99
00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:13.330
but I wanted to find something that felt like a job

100
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.010
that had the hours and being in the same place.

101
00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.610
A lot of the things that our other jobs

102
00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.230
that just didn't allow.

103
00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.180
The fact that you have prioritized your children,

104
00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.420
you'll never regret that.

105
00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.250
I had to do that with my children too.

106
00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:29.540
That's one of the reasons I went to Vegas for 11 years.

107
00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.750
And that was my point,

108
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:34.870
is that you found a job that put your kids first

109
00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.020
and when I heard that, it made me feel like I just,

110
00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.190
it made a lot of sense to me

111
00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.330
'cause it made me feel

112
00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.850
less alone.
And hey,

113
00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.420
I didn't make as much on the road

114
00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.510
when I was doing all my country touring,

115
00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.020
because I took all my kids with me and I have eight.

116
00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.620
And so, it's not great for airplane tickets and costs,

117
00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.410
